.env

# The SQLite DB was committed to git, so every deploy reset production data
# (posts, active-draft tracking, no-repeat memory) back to an old snapshot.
# That's what caused post #7 to get published instead of #8 — Railway checked
# out this stale file, including a stale "active_post_id" pointer, on every
# fresh deploy. Untracking it stops that; a Railway volume is still needed
# for real persistence across deploys (see chat).
jayesh_agent.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
